  "reference": "Galatians 6",
  "verseCount": 18,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "6",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "GAL 6"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "6",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Brethren, even if a man be overtaken in any trespass, ye who are spiritual, restore such a one in a spirit of gentleness; looking to thyself, lest thou also be tempted. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bear ye one another’s burdens, and so fulfil the law of Christ. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For if a man thinketh himself to be something when he is nothing, he deceiveth himself. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But let each man prove his own work, and then shall he have his glorying in regard of himself alone, and not of his neighbor. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For each man shall bear his own burden.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.5"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But let him that is taught in the word communicate unto him that teacheth in all good things. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Be not deceived; God is not mocked: for whatsoever a man soweth, that shall he also reap. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For he that soweth unto his own flesh shall of the flesh reap corruption; but he that soweth unto the Spirit shall of the Spirit reap eternal life. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And let us not be weary in well-doing: for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So then, as we have opportunity, let us work that which is good toward all men, and especially toward them that are of the household of the faith.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.10"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "See with how large letters I write unto you with mine own hand. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As many as desire to make a fair show in the flesh, they compel you to be circumcised; only that they may not be persecuted for the cross of Christ. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For not even they who receive circumcision do themselves keep the law; but they desire to have you circumcised, that they may glory in your flesh. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But far be it from me to glory, save in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ, through which the world hath been crucified unto me, and I unto the world. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For neither is circumcision anything, nor uncircumcision, but a new creature. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And as many as shall walk by this rule, peace ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " upon them, and mercy, and upon the Israel of God.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Henceforth let no man trouble me; for I bear branded on my body the marks of Jesus.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GAL 6:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit, brethren. Amen.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GAL.6.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GAL.6.18"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
